        "abstract": "In this paper we generalise the SIDH fault attack and the SIDH loop-abort fault attacks on supersingular isogeny cryptosystems (genus-1) to genus-2. Genus-2 isogeny-based cryptosystems are generalisations of its genus-1 counterpart, as such, attacks on the the latter are believed to generalise to the former.The point perturbation attack on supersingular elliptic curve isogeny cryptography has been shown to be practical. We show in this paper that this fault attack continues to be practical in genus-2, albeit with a few additional traces required. We also show that the loop-abort attack carries over to the genus-2 setting seamlessly.",
